<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Overview</h2>
<p>
    Python Finance ML Analytics is a portfolio-ready Jupyter notebook project focused on financial data analysis
    and machine-learning comparison. The work analyzes Microsoft alongside technology-sector peer companies,
    combines public market, financial, and macroeconomic data sources, and turns the results into visualizations,
    regression models, and written interpretation.
</p>
<p>
    The project began as university data science coursework and was later expanded with machine-learning techniques
    before being cleaned up as a public portfolio repository. The notebook focuses on Microsoft and peer technology
    companies, moving from valuation and revenue analysis into macroeconomic questions and model comparison while
    keeping the written interpretation close to the code and visual evidence.
</p>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Project Outcome</h2>
<p>
    The finished portfolio version shows an end-to-end analytics workflow: live public data retrieval, fallback handling
    for inconsistent data sources, financial metric preparation, visual analysis, regression model comparison, and
    written findings that explain both the results and the limits of the analysis.
</p>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Academic Context And Feedback</h2>
<p>
    The notebook grew out of two Spring 2025 COP3045 university assignments: a finance-focused data science project using
    Python, pandas, Matplotlib, and yfinance, followed by a machine-learning extension using scikit-learn.
    The finance analytics submission earned 105/100, and the machine-learning extension earned 100/100.
</p>
<aside class="border-start ps-3 mb-3 text-muted">
